naa_param — third-party data notice
===================================

This package and its repository contain NO third-party force-field data: no
published residue library, no published parameter set.

Libraries are obtained by the user — from their authors, or from the user's own
AmberTools installation — and imported with `naa-param import-library`, which
converts them into the user's own data directory ($NAA_PARAM_LIBRARY_DIR, else
~/.local/share/naa-param/libraries). The terms under which a library is
distributed bind the user who obtained it; the importer records the library's
citation and stated terms, and the SHA-256 of every file it read.

What the package does contain about published libraries is descriptive only:
for a few of them (naa_param/residues/sources.py, PRESETS), the parent force
fields they were fitted for, how their protonation states are named, whom to
cite and where to obtain them. No parameter is part of that description.

The parent force field
----------------------

naa_param reads the parent force field (e.g. amber99sb-ildn.ff, distributed
with GROMACS) from the user's installation and writes a modified copy of it; it
does not ship one.

AmberTools
----------

No AmberTools source code is included, linked or derived from: this package
invokes tleap, antechamber, parmchk2, espgen and resp as external programs.

Project data
------------

naa_param/params/consensus/ holds only data this project derives itself
(`naa-param calibrate`).

See docs/licences.md for details.
